This belongs in `libs/utils/nodeUtils.ts` `NodeUtils` class. Then we'll call it in a new function here

```typescript
private getFetchOptions() {
    return NodeUtils.getProxyUrl() != null
      ? ({ dispatcher: new EnvHttpProxyAgent() } as RequestInit)
      : undefined;
  }
```

Building on the previous comment, we can re-write this as:
```typescript
import { NodeUtils } from "@/libs/utils/nodeUtils";

...

  private init() {
    this.client = Client.init({
      fetchOptions: this.getFetchOptions(),
      ...
    });
  }
```

We can add another function in `NodeUtils` for this too:
```typescript
static getProxyAgent(): HttpsProxyAgent<string> | undefined {
    const proxyUrl = NodeUtils.getProxyUrl();
    return proxyUrl != null ? new HttpsProxyAgent(proxyUrl) : undefined;
  }
```
and this line just becomes
```typescript
agent: NodeUtils.getProxyAgent()
```

This will also let us consolidate this check in `NodeApiService`'s `nativeFetch`:
```typescript
nativeFetch(request: Request): Promise<Response> {
    (request as any).agent = NodeUtils.getProxyAgent();
    return fetch(request);
  }
```
Can you please make this change too?
